nd doesn’t prematurely advance into the center like e7.\n\nReason:  \nK: d8-e8 is the safest retreat, maintains flexibility, and allows for potential activation of the h8-rook via ...Rd8 in the future. It avoids centralizing the king when under pressure from the enemy queen.\n\nAnswer: K: d8-e8'}
